>I've had cases where I randomly polymorph out of the blue.  It's not a trap
>because I can step back on the square and have nothing happen.  I'm not
>wearing a ring of polymorph, either.  Why does this happen and how can I
>prevent it?  I lost a good Samurai character this way; I though my +5 Hawaiian
>shirt was safe underneath my armor.  :-(

Polymorph traps are one of the least understood elements of Nethack, for
some reason. If you step on a polymorph trap, you polymorph and the trap
disappears. (This leads a lot of people to say that "I polymorphed, but
it wasn't because of a trap," which is incorrect.) If something other than
you steps on the trap, they polymorph, but it doesn't disappear. Since
searching is never 100% effective and very few people search before each and
every step, it's not possible to ever be certain you haven't stepped on a
trap. Conversely, if you polymorph and didn't intend to it's a sure bet that
either you're wearing a ring of polymorph or you stepped on a polymorph
trap (or you ate a chameleon corpse, but that's pretty obvious.)




